{"step_index":2027,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-03T08:38:11Z","content":"# Resuming from a compaction\n\nYou are continuing work on the task described above, but you have lost access to the full conversation history, and need to resume work efficiently using the progress summary below:\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. CRITICAL FIX: Stop parsing invoice headers, PAN cards, and bank details as line items.\n\n1. UPDATE GEMINI EXTRACTION PROMPT:\n\"You are a strict GST Invoice extractor. \nRULES FOR LINE ITEMS:\n- Extract items ONLY from the central itemized table bounded between the table header (S.No, Description, HSN, Qty, Rate, Amount) and the Subtotal row.\n- NEVER extract text from the header or footer as line items:\n  * DO NOT extract addresses or cities (e.g. 'Mumbai, Maharashtra').\n  * DO NOT extract PAN, GSTIN, or buyer details (e.g. 'PAN : 26CORPP').\n  * DO NOT extract bank account or payment details (e.g. 'Acc. Number 271').\n- Each valid line item MUST have a legitimate product name, quantity > 0, unit rate > 0, and total amount.\n\nGRAND TOTAL:\n- Extract the final payable Grand Total printed at the bottom of the bill (e.g., '4,490.00' / 'FOUR THOUSAND FOUR HUNDRED AND NINETY'). Do NOT extract partial account numbers or phone numbers as the grand total.\"\n\n2. BACKEND FILTER:\nReject any item if its description contains 'PAN', 'Acc. Number', 'Account', 'Bank', 'IFSC', or standard state/city names like 'Maharashtra', 'Mumbai', 'Delhi', 'Haryana'.\n\n\n<truncated 760 bytes>\n2.  CRITICAL FIX: Billed Grand Total is extracting \"774\" instead of the actual printed total (4,489.90 / 4,490.00).\n\n1. UPDATE GEMINI EXTRACTION PROMPT:\n\"GRAND TOTAL PARSING RULES:\n- The Grand Total MUST be the overall final payable invoice amount, NOT a column entry, tax rate, or HSN fragment like '774'.\n- Logic check: Grand Total must be approximately (Subtotal + Total Tax). \n  Here, Subtotal is ~3,805 and IGST is ~684.90, so the Grand Total MUST be around 4,489.90 or 4,490.00.\n- If you see a small number like '774', it is an HSN code, partial tax, or serial number. DO NOT use it as `declared_total`.\n- Always look at the printed words: 'FOUR THOUSAND FOUR HUNDRED AND NINETY RUPEES' confirms the total is ~4,490.\"\n\n2. BACKEND FALLBACK LOGIC:\nIn your backend before sending to frontend:\n# If declared_total is suspiciously smaller than subtotal, reject the OCR hallucination:\nif data.get(\"declared_total\", 0) < (data.get(\"subtotal\", 0) * 0.5):\n    # Fallback to subtotal + total taxes\n    data[\"declared_total\"] = round(data.get(\"subtotal\", 0) + data.get(\"cgst\", 0) + data.get(\"sgst\", 0) + data.get(\"igst\", 0), 2)\n3. it still has 774 billed on invoice the issue is not fixed keeping the core features and the rest of the things untouched fix this error\n4. Support both AIzaSy API keys and AQ. OAuth/Bearer tokens in the Gemini backend and client calls:\n\n1. In the backend Gemini caller:\n   - Check the key format:\n     if api_key.startswith(\"AQ.\"):\n         # Treat as Google Cloud OAuth / Bearer Token\n         headers = {\n             \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {api_key}\",\n             \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"\n         }\n         # Call the Gemini v1beta REST endpoint directly via httpx or requests:\n         url = \"https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/gemini-2.5-flash:generateContent\"\n     else:\n         # Standard AIzaSy key passed via header or query param\n         headers = {\n             \"x-goog-api-key\": api_key,\n             \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"\n         }\n         url = \"https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/gemini-2.5-flash:generateContent\"\n\n2. Handle this authentication seamlessly so the backend doesn't return 401 when using an AQ. token.\n5. CRITICAL PARSER REFACTOR: IMPLEMENT 3-TIER PRODUCTION INVOICE EXTRACTION PIPELINE\n\nRefactor our invoice parsing pipeline across backend and client fallback to eliminate brittle line-by-line regex. Implement these 3 steps:\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSTEP 1: TABLE-ANCHOR BOUNDARY SLICING (in invoiceTextParser.js / parser logic)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nStop running OCR regex top-to-bottom across the entire document text. Instead, slice the document into 3 distinct vertical zones:\n1. HEADER ZONE (Top to Table Start):\n   - Start: Beginning of text.\n   - End: Table Header row containing at least two keywords: ['Description', 'Item', 'Particulars', 'HSN', 'Qty', 'Rate', 'Amount'].\n   - Purpose: Extract Vendor Name, GSTIN, Invoice Number, and Date ONLY.\n   - Guardrail: Never extract any line from this zone as an item, even if it contains numbers, addresses ('Shop No', 'Plot', 'Bazaar'), or phone numbers.\n\n2. LINE ITEM ZONE (Strict Table Boundaries):\n   - Start: Immediately after the Table Header row.\n   - End: Table Footer row \n<truncated 3322 bytes>\n6. FIX GST TAX EXTRACTION IN INVOICE PARSER:\n\n1. STOP CAPTURING ITEM QUANTITY/WATTAGE AS TAX:\n   - Do NOT search for generic two-digit numbers when extracting GST. '20' from '20W' or 'Pack of 20' must never be mapped to tax amounts.\n   - Tax extraction must look strictly for tax lines in the summary zone:\n     * CGST line pattern: /(?:CGST|Central GST)[\\s@%]*([0-9\\.]+)?%?[\\s:]*[₹\\s]*([0-9,]+(?:\\.[0-9]{2})?)/i\n     * SGST line pattern: /(?:SGST|State GST)[\\s@%]*([0-9\\.]+)?%?[\\s:]*[₹\\s]*([0-9,]+(?:\\.[0-9]{2})?)/i\n     * IGST line pattern: /(?:IGST|Integrated GST)[\\s@%]*([0-9\\.]+)?%?[\\s:]*[₹\\s]*([0-9,]+(?:\\.[0-9]{2})?)/i\n\n2. INTRA-STATE vs INTER-STATE AUTO-DETERMINATION:\n   - Compare the first 2 digits of the Supplier GSTIN (06) and Buyer GSTIN (06).\n   - If both state codes match (Intra-State):\n     * Set IGST strictly to 0.\n     * Default tax split to CGST + SGST (e.g. 9% + 9% = 18%, giving ₹990 CGST and ₹990 SGST on ₹11,000).\n   - If state codes differ (Inter-State):\n     * Set CGST = 0, SGST = 0, and IGST = 18% (₹1,980.00).\n\n3. CLICK HANDLER SYNC:\n   Ensure clicking the '[18% (Electrical)]' quick button recalculates C\n<truncated 220 bytes>\n7. CRITICAL FIX: GST Tax extraction is injecting 2990 into CGST/SGST instead of 990.\n\n1. FIX THE DEFAULT TAX AUTO-CALCULATION:\n   - When GST is 18% Intra-State on a subtotal of ₹11,000.00:\n     * CGST @ 9% = 990.00 (NOT 2990.00)\n     * SGST @ 9% = 990.00 (NOT 2990.00)\n     * IGST = 0.00\n     * Total Tax = 1,980.00\n   - NEVER hallucinate the tax by taking (Billed Total - Subtotal). Calculate tax strictly as:\n     tax = subtotal * (rate_percentage / 100).\n\n2. FIX REGEX EXTRACTION OF PRINTED TAX VALUES:\n   - Match the exact printed tax lines on the bill:\n     Search for \"CGST @ 9%\" -> extract 990.00\n     Search for \"SGST @ 9%\" -> extract 990.00\n   - Ensure the regex does not prepend a stray '2' (e.g. from state code '06' or line 2) to the number '990.00'.\n\n3. MAKE QUICK GST BUTTONS AUTOCALCULATE:\n   - Clicking '[18% (Electrical)]' should immediately set:\n     cgst = subtotal * 0.09;\n     sgst = subtotal * 0.09;\n     igst = 0;\n   - Trigger the math recalculation immediately so Verified Total becomes 12,980.00.\n\nKEEP ALL EXISTING UI LAYOUT, SEC 44AD ITR-4 INSIGHTS, AND TABLE CONTROLS UNTOUCHED. \n8. FEATURE: DEDICATED \"Tax & ITR Filing\" TAB WITH FULLY CUSTOMIZABLE TAX ENGINE\n\nAdd a tab navigation bar to the invoice review view to switch between:\n- Tab 1: [🧾 Invoice Math Audit] (Current verification screen)\n- Tab 2: [📊 Tax & ITR Filing] (New customizable tax & compliance dashboard)\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTAB 1: [🧾 Invoice Math Audit]\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nKeep everything currently in this view UNTOUCHED:\n- PDF / image preview on the left.\n- Interactive line-item table, edit inputs, and real-time math engine.\n- Billed on Invoice, Verified Total, and Overcharge / Match warning cards.\n- GST split inputs and quick percentage buttons.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTAB 2: [📊 Tax & ITR Filing] (CUSTOMIZABLE TAX ENGINE)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBuild a flexible, interactive tax planning view that lets the shopkeeper adjust their own parameters:\n\n1. REGIME & FILING TYPE SELECTOR (Customizable Mode):\n  \n<truncated 2481 bytes>\n9. INTEGRATION: WIRE TAB 2 (TAX & ITR FILING) INTO APP.JS WITH REACTIVE TAB SWITCHER\n\nConnect the newly created `TaxAndITRTab` component into `app.js` with a top-level tab switcher.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1. COMPONENT IMPORT (app.js):\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nImport the new component at the top of `app.js`:\nimport TaxAndITRTab from './components/TaxAndITRTab'; // Ensure path matches your structure\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n2. STATE MANAGEMENT (app.js):\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAdd an active tab state hook inside the main App component:\nconst [activeTab, setActiveTab] = useState('audit'); // 'audit' | 'tax'\n\nEnsure the active tab defaults to 'audit' upon uploading a new bill or resetting.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3. TOP NAVIGATION SWITCHER BAR:\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPlace this tab switcher bar imme\n<truncated 17816 bytes>\n10. REFACTOR: REMOVE INLINE TAX CARD AND BUILD STORED BILLS TAX LEDGER TAB\n\n1. CLEAN UP TAB 1 (Invoice Math Audit):\n- Completely delete/unmount the dark card at the bottom right: \"Tax & ITR Insights Sec 44AD Presumptive\" along with the 3 pills, digital receipts slider, and the Gemini tax callout.\n- Keep only:\n  * Live Tax Invoice Preview (left)\n  * Audit Verdict & Diff cards (top right)\n  * Bill Header Inputs (Supplier Name, GSTIN, Billed Grand Total)\n  * Item Breakdown & Math Check table\n  * GST Tax Rate & Split box\n  * Action buttons ([📋 Copy Note], [📲 WhatsApp], [📑 CA Audit Slip])\n- Add an explicit button in the action bar:\n  [💾 Save Bill to Tax Ledger]\n  Clicking this saves the current verified bill into local/indexed storage (or backend DB) and updates the ledger.\n\n2. BUILD TAB 2 (Tax & ITR Filing) AS AN ACCUMULATIVE LEDGER & TAX ENGINE:\nWhen switching to the \"📊 Tax & ITR Filing\" tab, display a full business ledger instead of an inline single-invoice card:\n\nA. STORED INVOICE BILLS TABLE:\n- Display a table listing all saved bills:\n  * Columns: Date, Invoice No., Supplier Name, GSTIN, Taxable Subtotal, CGST, SGST, I\n<truncated 1943 bytes>\n\n<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **User's Core Request:**\n  1. **Clean up Tab 1 (Invoice Math Audit):**\n     - Completely delete/unmount the dark card at bottom right: \"Tax & ITR Insights Sec 44AD Presumptive\" along with the 3 pills, digital receipts slider, and Gemini tax callout.\n     - Keep only: Live Tax Invoice Preview (left), Audit Verdict & Diff cards (top right), Bill Header Inputs, Item Breakdown & Math Check table, GST Tax Rate & Split box, Action buttons (`[📋 Copy Note]`, `[📲 WhatsApp]`, `[📑 CA Audit Slip]`).\n     - Add explicit button in action bar: `[💾 Save Bill to Tax Ledger]`. Clicking saves the current verified bill into persistent storage (`localStorage`) and updates the ledger.\n  2. **Build Tab 2 (Tax & ITR Filing) as an Accumulative Ledger & Tax Engine:**\n     - **A. Stored Invoice Bills Table:** List saved bills with columns (Date, Invoice No., Supplier Name, GSTIN, Taxable Subtotal, CGST, SGST, IGST, Verified Total, Actions: View / Delete). Summary Bar across stored bills (Total Bills Verified: N, Total Purchase Expenditure (Cost of Goods): ₹[Sum of Subtotals], Total Claimable GST ITC: ₹[Sum of Taxes]).\n     - **B. Aggregated GST ITC Ledger (GSTR-3B Preparation):** Pools for CGST, SGST, IGST. Statutory compliance check (flags missing/invalid supplier GSTINs, 180-day vendor payment timeline under Section 16).\n     - **C. Customizable Annual Business & ITR Calculator (ITR-4 / ITR-3):** Inputs for Annual Gross Sales/Turnover (default ₹30,00,000), Mode Toggle: `[Presumptive Sec 44AD (ITR-4)]` vs `[Normal P&L (ITR-3)]`.\n       - Mode 44AD: Digital Receipts % slider (default 80%), customizable profit rates (6% digital, 8% cash).\n       - Normal P&L: Purchase costs auto-populated from Total Purchase Expenditure of saved bills (editable), Operating expenses input, Net Profit = Gross Sales - (Purchases + Opex).\n       - Live Tax Liability Summary: New Tax Regime slabs (FY 2025-26), Section 87A rebate evaluation (₹0 Tax Payable if within ceiling), Section 44AB tax audit check.\n     - **D. Data Management:** `[📥 Export Consolidated Tax & ITC Summary (CSV / PDF)]` and `[🗑️ Clear All Stored Bills]`.\n- **Scope Guard:**\n  - Do NOT alter OCR extraction logic, reverse-token parser, or table math calculations in Tab 1. Simply wire verified bill data to persist into Tab 2 ledger upon clicking `[💾 Save Bill to Tax Ledger]`.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Completed:**\n  - [x] **`components/AuditScorecard.js`**:\n    - Deleted lines 541–665 (the dark card \"Tax & ITR Insights Sec 44AD Presumptive\", 3 pills, digital slider, Gemini advisory callout).\n    - Updated action buttons to include `[💾 Save Bill to Tax Ledger]`.\n    - Added `onSaveToLedger` prop to `renderAuditScorecard` and wired `#btn-save-to-ledger` click listener.\n    - Removed orphaned `btnRefreshTax` and `sliderDigital` event listeners.\n  - [x] **`components/ReviewWorkspace.js`**:\n    - Wired `onSaveToLedger: options.onSaveToLedger` in `renderAuditScorecard` call.\n    - Added `options.hideInternalTabs` guard so only the top-level switcher bar in `app.js` is rendered.\n  - [x] **`components/TaxAndITRTab.js`**:\n    - Completely rewritten into the full accumulative business ledger and tax engine:\n      * Stored invoice bills table with View / Delete actions.\n      * Top summary cards (Total Bills Verified, Total Purchases COGS, Total Claimable ITC).\n      * Aggregated GST ITC pools (CGST, SGST, IGST), Section 16(2) GSTIN validation, 180-day vendor rule.\n      * Mode B (Sec 44AD) vs Mode A (Normal P&L with purchase costs auto-filled from ledger total).\n      * Section 87A full rebate status & Section 44AB tax audit threshold check.\n      * `exportConsolidatedTaxCsv` and print handlers.\n      * Clear ledger button with confirmation.\n  - [x] **`routes/tax_advisory.py` & `server.py`**:\n    - Created FastAPI router with `POST /api/tax/calculate-advisory` using `TaxCalculationRequest` and `TaxCalculationResponse`.\n    - Registered `tax_router` in `server.py`.\n- **In Progress / Pending:**\n  - Update `app.js` to manage `this.savedBills`:\n    - Initialize `this.savedBills` from `localStorage.getItem(\"audit_it_tax_ledger_bills\")` (seeding with current sample if empty so user immediately sees a working ledger).\n    - Implement `handleSaveBillToLedger(invoice, audit)` that persists verified bills to `localStorage` and shows a toast.\n    - Wire `renderTaxAndITRTab` in `app.js` with `savedBills`, `onViewBill`, `onDeleteBill`, `onClearBills`, and `onSaveCurrentBill`.\n    - Connect `onSaveToLedger: (inv, aud) => this.handleSaveBillToLedger(inv, aud)` into `renderReviewWorkspace`.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings\n- Tab 1 is now completely clean: only shows invoice preview, audit scorecard, table check, GST rate/splits, and action buttons (`[💾 Save Bill to Tax Ledger]`, `[📋 Copy Note]`, `[📲 WhatsApp]`, `[📑 CA Slip]`, `[← Back]`).\n- When `onViewBill(bill)` is triggered from Tab 2, `app.js` should set `this.currentInvoice = bill`, run `this.currentAudit = auditInvoice(bill)`, set `this.activeTab = \"audit\"`, and call `this.render()` to let the user inspect the bill in Tab 1.\n- In `Normal P&L (ITR-3)` mode, auto-populating purchase costs from `totalPurchases` of the stored bills ledger gives a seamless connection between audited receipts and business expenditure.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Errors & Fixes\n1. *Error:* Target content mismatch when modifying `components/TaxAndITRTab.js`.\n   - *Fix:* Read exact line numbers (255-310) and replaced `setupHandlers` cleanly with the complete parameter set.\n2. *Error:* Port 3000 socket permissions in sandbox when testing endpoints directly via urllib.\n   - *Fix:* Used Starlette `TestClient(app)` to run ASGI in-process tests without hitting network permission boundaries.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Active Context\n- **Workspace Directory:** `/Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it`\n- **Active Background Daemon:**\n  - Task ID: `f7fe8eca-ba38-4dcb-97a7-a40aeb890237/task-1915`\n  - Command: `./venv/bin/python3 server.py 3000`\n  - Port: `3000`\n\n---\n\n### 6. Next Steps\n1. **Update `app.js`**:\n   - In constructor, load `this.savedBills` from `localStorage.getItem(\"audit_it_tax_ledger_bills\")`. If empty, seed with `SAMPLE_INVOICES['clean']` (Modern Electrical & Hardware) so the ledger starts with 1 verified bill.\n   - Add method `handleSaveBillToLedger(invoice, audit)`:\n     - Formats bill object (`id`, `invoice_no`, `date`, `vendor_name`, `gstin`, `subtotal`, `cgst`, `sgst`, `igst`, `total_tax`, `verified_total`, `status`, `items`).\n     - Updates existing record if matching `invoice_no` exists, else unshifts new record.\n     - Saves to `localStorage.setItem(\"audit_it_tax_ledger_bills\", JSON.stringify(this.savedBills))`.\n     - Displays `this.showToast(...)`.\n   - In `render()` when `this.currentView === \"review\"`:\n     - In Tab 1 (`renderReviewWorkspace`), pass `onSaveToLedger: (inv, aud) => this.handleSaveBillToLedger(inv, aud)`.\n     - In Tab 2 (`renderTaxAndITRTab`), pass:\n       * `savedBills: this.savedBills`\n       * `currentInvoice: this.currentInvoice`\n       * `currentAudit: this.currentAudit`\n       * `state: this.taxTabState`\n       * `onUpdateState: (newState) => { this.taxTabState = { ...this.taxTabState, ...newState }; this.render(); }`\n       * `onViewBill: (bill) => { this.currentInvoice = bill; this.currentAudit = auditInvoice(bill); this.setActiveTab(\"audit\"); }`\n       * `onDeleteBill: (id) => { this.savedBills = this.savedBills.filter(b => (b.id || b.invoice_no) !== id); localStorage.setItem(\"audit_it_tax_ledger_bills\", JSON.stringify(this.savedBills)); this.render(); }`\n       * `onClearBills: () => { this.savedBills = []; localStorage.removeItem(\"audit_it_tax_ledger_bills\"); this.render(); }`\n       * `onSaveCurrentBill: () => this.handleSaveBillToLedger(this.currentInvoice, this.currentAudit)`\n2. **Verify with in-process TestClient & Node tests**:\n   - Verify all routes return 200 OK.\n   - Verify `TaxAndITRTab.js`, `AuditScorecard.js`, and `app.js` compile and execute without error.\n3. **Notify User**:\n   - Report the clean-up of Tab 1, the new `[💾 Save Bill to Tax Ledger]` button, and the accumulative Tab 2 ledger with clickable `file://` links.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- Do NOT alter OCR extraction logic, reverse-token parser, or table math calculations in Tab 1.\n- Provide clickable `file://` links for all edited files and components.\n</summary>\n\n# Running Background Tasks\nThe following background tasks were running at the time this checkpoint was created.\nUse the manage_task tool to interact with them (e.g. to kill them or check their status).\n\n{\n  \"taskId\":  \"f7fe8eca-ba38-4dcb-97a7-a40aeb890237/task-1915\",\n  \"toolName\":  \"run_command\",\n  \"toolSummary\":  \"Restart FastAPI server with tax advisory router\",\n  \"description\":  \"/Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity